<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">hexes</ansi>

A hex is a Witch's spell that takes enemy turns away instead of dealing
damage (<ansi fg="command">help witch</ansi>). It puts a status on a foe (<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>). Hexes belong to
the hexcraft school, which only a Witch may learn.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The hexes</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Hex</ansi>               <ansi fg="yellow">level</ansi>  <ansi fg="yellow">mana</ansi>  <ansi fg="yellow">chant</ansi>  <ansi fg="yellow">what it does</ansi>
  Slumber             1      6     2     asleep for 2 rounds: loses its turns, and
                                         the first damage wakes it (blows against a
                                         sleeper hit 25 points more often)
  Withering Hex       1      8     2     a weak damage curse, for when no hex is
                                         worth casting
  Earthbind           3      6     2     knocked down: loses its next action and is
                                         easier to hit
  Leaden Curse        5      8     2     hobbled: slow, and unable to flee
  Miasma              7     10     3     poisons one row of foes; Cure Poison ends it
  Binding Hex        10     12     3     paralyzed for 1 round, 2 from level 20:
                                         loses its turns and can't dodge or block;
                                         damage does not break it. Resisted with
                                         Vitality
  Curse of Frailty   12     10     2     exposed: blows against it crit far more
                                         often
  Dread Whisper      15     14     3     one morale check on the foe, which may yield
                                         or flee (<ansi fg="command">help morale</ansi>); a Witch never
                                         casts it at an unbreakable foe
  Blight             18     12     2     healing it receives is halved for 3 rounds;
                                         cast only at enemy healers

A Witch learns a hex when it reaches its level, and keeps it for good.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How many foes a hex reaches</ansi>

A hex reaches 1 foe at level 1, <ansi fg="yellow">2</ansi> at level 8, <ansi fg="yellow">3</ansi> at level 16, <ansi fg="yellow">4</ansi> at level 24,
and the whole enemy group from level 30. The first is the one it aims at;
the rest come from the same row, then the nearest others. Miasma covers one
row only, up to the same number. In a battle the Witch chooses on her own.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Resisting</ansi>

Each foe resists on its own. The Witch's Mysticism is set against the foe's
Mysticism (its Vitality, for Binding Hex): the hex lands 65 times in 100 at
equal stats, one more for every point of Mysticism the Witch has over the foe's,
never under 25 or over 90. A boss resists 25 more, and a status holds it half
as long, rounding down to at least 1 round. A resisted hex does nothing, and the
line says <ansi fg="command">(resisted)</ansi>; a foe already under a hex isn't hexed again.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">No endless holds</ansi>

After a hex lands, that foe can't be put to sleep, paralyzed or knocked down
again (any of the three) until the status has been over for 2 combat rounds,
and no other hex is cast twice at it in that time either. So no foe loses
more than half of a fight's rounds to hexes. (A Wise One's or Coven Mother's
longer holds are followed by as long an immunity, so the half still stands.)
Sleep ends at the first damage; poison's damage does too.

Statuses count combat rounds, never game rounds, and end when the fight ends.
Miasma's poison is ordinary poison: it runs its course, in or out of a
fight, unless Cure Poison ends it.
<ansi fg="command">help spell [spell]</ansi> shows one spell's numbers.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help witch</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help mana</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help spells</ansi>.
